    "question_type": "single_choice",
    "question": "When the polynomial P(x) = 2x^3 - 5x^2 + ax - 8 is divided by (x - 2), the remainder is 6. What is the value of the constant a?",
    "options": [
      "5",
      "7",
      "9",
      "11"
    ],
    "answer": "9",
    "explanation": "By the Remainder Theorem, the remainder when P(x) is divided by (x - 2) is P(2). P(2) = 2(2^3) - 5(2^2) + a(2) - 8 = 2(8) - 5(4) + 2a - 8 = 16 - 20 + 2a - 8 = 2a - 12. Given P(2) = 6: 2a - 12 = 6 => 2a = 18 => a = 9.",
